 ggml-backend-meta.cpp), the view slot is bound for EVERY graph build/alloc
 (not only on an alt-state change), and the async-input ring waits per ORIGIN
 stream instead of cudaDeviceSynchronize (illegal while a peer arm captures a
 graph -- measured 'operation not permitted when stream is capturing')

Validated: the 71k/23k/800 three-slot shape, 3 rounds clean (0 asserts, 0 ROCm errors, 0 segfaults);
pair OFF clean; gate-arms-soak.sh soak --quick PASS 11/11 including the class-matched text oracle.
Still blocked on the host tier (-ncmoe 48): a pre-existing abort in ggml_cuda_pool_vmm::alloc's peer grant
(cuMemSetAccess 'invalid argument'), pair-only, needs the best-effort-grant treatment the slab already has.
