From 431365ec5574cde39da2e3b75aa36d9a001f1257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:36:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] crash #373 fix (candidate), part 4 + TODO #366: the
 synchronous host paths stop using the cudaStreamPerThread sentinel, and the
 pair's slab reserve is derived from the ubatch width

(1) ggml_cuda_host_stream(): one private non-blocking stream per (thread, device) for every SYNCHRONOUS host<->device
path (set/get tensor, memset, the bounce and peer-staging copies, the KV-region row moves) -- 53 sites.  HIP maps
cudaStreamPerThread onto the legacy DEFAULT stream, which a peer context's graph capture claims device-wide, so a host
copy from the other arm of the pair is refused: measured as 'operation not permitted when stream is capturing' in
llm_graph_input_ple::set_input on the host tier, i.e. the same class as the async-input ring.  The async ring's origin
now uses that same stream, so the ordering the sentinel used to provide (a get_tensor syncs the stream a queued upload
will run on) is preserved.

(2) #366: common_arms_dec_reserve() derives the pair's slab reserve instead of returning the flat 3584 MiB -- the flat
floor plus a WIDTH-keyed tier (0 at -ub <= 1024, 1536 MiB at >= 2048, +256 per doubling) for the prefill arm's
post-prefill narrow re-reserve, which is the second late narrow view the pair creates.  Measured (Flash-Next, -ncmoe 48,
-c 131072, arena 13.3 GiB, 3 slots, 71k+23k+800, 2 rounds): 3584 fails, 4096 fails, 5120 CLEAN -- and 5120 is what the
derivation now prints ('aux=5.00 GiB'), so the host tier needs no knob.  Resident config and the soak gate unaffected.

Also found: the gate's 'pool' arm is VACUOUS (no expert-access census) both with and without this change -- recorded as
a gate defect, not accepted.
---
 common/common.cpp               |  48 ++++++++++-
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu | 148 ++++++++++++++++++--------------
 2 files changed, 130 insertions(+), 66 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/common.cpp b/common/common.cpp
