@@ -1335,15 +1335,59 @@ common_gguf_info common_get_gguf_info(const std::string & fname) {
 // margin this file's other reserves take.  `MOE_EXPERT_CACHE_AUX_RESERVE_MIB` overrides it for both cases.
 #define LLAMA_ARMS_DEC_RESERVE_MIB_DEFAULT 3584  // the same flat second-context reserve an embedded MTP head gets
 
+// TODO #366: the pair creates a SECOND late narrow (decode/verify-width) compute view as well -- the prefill arm
+// re-reserves one after every wide prefill (`process_ubatch`'s post-prefill drop), and it lands after the arena has
+// been re-armed.  That view is the same tier as the decode context's own (`-ub 2048` on the largest model here:
+// 1430.16 and 1430.63 MiB, i.e. the same layout), so the flat reserve is charged ONE MORE of it.  The tier is a
+// measured FLOOR, rounded up to the reserve granularity this file uses, and the direction of the rounding is
+// deliberately upward: over-estimating costs little (the surplus is reclaimed into the arena by `slab_extend` when
+// the late views leave more than `headroom` outside), while under-estimating aborts a request
+// (`graph_reserve: failed to allocate compute buffers` -> `failed to allocate graph`).
