From fdc58fc7890fab1a05a64e4ac5eb30e091b33293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:34:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] TODO #365: the Meta buffer gets a per-child, split-aware
 `cpy_tensor_n` -- a `-sm tensor` hybrid's state handover is a device copy
 (1.4-3.3 ms) instead of a 112.57 MiB host round trip (72-77 ms)

`llama_memory_recurrent::seq_state_take()` hands one sequence's recurrent rows between the two arms of the
prefill/decode pair as ONE `ggml_backend_tensor_copy_n()` over 2-D row views it builds OUT OF GRAPH; those views are
registered in no simple-tensor container, and the Meta buffer exposed neither `cpy_tensor` nor `cpy_tensor_n`, so
`can_take_batched()` refused the batched take and every boundary on a `-sm tensor` hybrid took the serialised
fallback (`state_write()` -> host -> `state_read()`): 112.57 MiB, 72-77 ms, in TTFT.

The hook is per CHILD: the split state of the view's ROOT (the tensor the memory allocated, which IS registered) says
which byte range of a row belongs to which child, and each child's own buffer takes a plain copy of its rows --
both sides are children of the SAME layout, so a child's covered rows are one contiguous range even when the split
state is segmented/repeated (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next's state is one segment repeated 3 or 5 times, i.e. the chunks are
interleaved inside the row on both sides, identically).  A shape the planner cannot express that way is staged
through the host via the root, never partially copied.  `cpy_tensor` (the single-tensor hook) stays null on purpose:
`can_copy_tensor()` is satisfied by either hook, the take only uses the batched one, and the single-tensor hook would
silently reroute the KV-park and state-staging copies that take the host path today.

`LLAMA_RS_VERIFY_TAKE=1` now instruments WHICHEVER arm runs (it used to see only the serialised fallback), and
`LLAMA_RS_VERIFY_TAKE_DUMP=<file>` appends each verified destination blob so two arms can be compared with cmp(1).

Measured (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ4_NL, 3 devices, `-sm tensor`, the maintainer's shape):
  * take 1.4-1.9 ms interleaved (3.0-3.3 ms with the verify capture), first take in a process ~5.5 ms, against
    72-77 ms serialised -- 40-50x, and it no longer lands in TTFT;
  * VERIFY: 0 of 118 039 420 byte(s) differ (cell metadata included) -- FAITHFUL;
  * the same turn driven SERIAL + ARM_TEMP=0 once per arm: the per-take destination dumps are BYTE-IDENTICAL
    (708 236 592 B, 6 takes) and all three requests' generated text is byte-identical;
  * `gate-ckpt-reuse.sh` PASS on 1 GPU `-sm layer` and on 3 GPUs `-sm tensor`, `gate-state-pipe.sh` PASS,
    `gate-arms-soak.sh soak --quick` PASS 11/11 with the text oracle.
